p='proof_template_exec.md'
t=open(p).read()
def rep(a,b):
    global t
    assert t.count(a)==1,(a[:60],t.count(a)); t=t.replace(a,b)
rep("`nolibc.c` (section 9) supplies the process entry, the system calls `write`, `mmap`, `munmap`, `clock_gettime` and `exit_group`, `memcpy`, `memset`, `memmove`, `strcmp`, `log2` and the small `printf` of the report lines; there is no loader, no shared library and no other library code. Three terms are counted.",
    "`nolibc.c` (section 9) supplies the process entry, the two system calls the program executes (`write`, once, and `exit_group`, once), `memcpy`, `memset`, `memmove`, `strcmp`, `log2` and the small `printf` that appends the report to one buffer; there is no loader, no shared library, no other library code and no other system call. Three terms make up the memory.")
i=t.index("(b) The footprint of the memory taken from the kernel")
j=t.index("\n",i)
t=t[:i]+"(b) The heap is inside term (a): every buffer of the program is served by `xalloc` from one static arena of `@@ARENA@@` bytes in the bss (`ARENA` in `common.h`, a multiple of 64; the bss of the image is `@@BSS@@` bytes and contains it together with the 8,192-byte output buffer and the other static state). Nothing is mapped from the kernel at run time. The arena is exactly the extent the recorded run needed: the highest end address of any block over the whole run was `@@EXTENT@@` bytes (`ARENA size=... extent=...` in the run output), and the run would have stopped with status 2 if a request had not fitted. Each block has a 64-byte header (size, size of the previous block, in-use flag; it keeps the payload 64-byte aligned) and a payload rounded up to a multiple of 64 bytes; the allocator is described, with its charges, in section 4.2. At the peak of the bytes in use (stage D) there were @@PEAK_LIVE@@ live blocks holding @@PEAK_PAY@@ bytes of payload; their @@PEAK_LIVE@@ headers of 64 bytes (@@HDR@@ bytes) are inside the figure of @@HEAP_PEAK@@ bytes in use. The largest buffers (stage C at `m = @@M@@`) are the twiddle table (`2^@@TWEXP@@` elements, @@TWB@@ bytes), `Y` (`3 * 2^@@AEXP@@` elements, @@YB@@), `tmp` (`2^@@AEXP@@` elements, @@TMPB@@), `MU` (@@MUB@@), `g` (@@GB@@) and the result `F` (@@FB@@). Peaks of bytes in use per stage (maximum over the trials): @@STAGE_PEAKS@@."+t[j:]
rep("Not counted: the pages the kernel maps for a process outside its executable image (the vdso and vvar mappings, page tables) and the kernel's buffers for the report written with `write`. As a cross-check,",
    "The pages the kernel itself maps for a process outside its executable image (the vdso and vvar mappings, page tables) and the kernel's buffer for the one `write` are the kernel's memory and lie outside the program's memory figure. As a cross-check,")
rep("(about @@SECS@@ s; the footprint of section 7 is the page-rounded mapped size and does not depend on any library)","(about @@SECS@@ s of user time; the memory of section 7 is the size of the image and does not depend on any library)")
rep("Nothing is bounded, extrapolated or taken from another run: every figure below is a counter of the same execution.","Every figure below is a counter of the same execution, or a stated constant charged in the stage that executes the thing it covers (stage I, section 4.2); nothing is taken from another run. The meter itself, the increments of the counters `X` and `fp_cnt` that record the charges, is how the rules are applied, not a step of the program.")
rep("the program prints one total","the program prints one total") if False else None
rep("Total `N = @@N@@` operations (stage rows, trial rows plus the row outside the trials, and the counters of the run, all equal)","Total `N = @@N@@` operations, including stage I (the stage rows, the trial rows plus the row outside the trials, and the counters of the run, all equal; the one total printed in the report is this `N`)")
open(p,'w').write(t)
n=open('note_template.md').read()
def rn(a,b):
    global n
    assert n.count(a)==1,(a[:60],n.count(a)); n=n.replace(a,b)
rn("The output itself is part of the run: stage H converts the two pairs, the digest and the centre to canonical form and encodes them as hexadecimal text, 12 operations per digit, inside the total.",
   "The output itself is part of the run and inside the total: stage H converts the two pairs, the digest and the centre to canonical form and encodes them as hexadecimal text, 12 operations per digit; stage I charges the formatting of the whole report (an upper bound of 256 operations per byte for the full 8,192-byte output buffer, 2,097,152), the single write system call (10,000 + 8 per buffer byte), the single exit system call (10,000), the loops of the report, the bookkeeping of the stages (1,000 per stage) and the entry code. The allocator is charged load by load, store by store, comparison by comparison, inside the stages that call it.")
i=n.index("Memory. The executable")
j=n.index("\n",i)
n=n[:i]+"Memory. The executable is linked statically and without any C library (a small runtime, nolibc.c, supplies the entry code, the two system calls write and exit_group, memcpy/memset and the report printing); its whole image is counted: @@STATIC_BYTES@@ bytes (text, data and bss). The heap is inside that figure: every buffer comes from one static arena of @@ARENA@@ bytes in the bss (a first-fit allocator with a 64-byte header per block and merging of free neighbours; no mmap and no munmap), exactly the extent the run needed (@@EXTENT@@ bytes). At the peak of use there were @@PEAK_LIVE@@ blocks, payload @@PEAK_PAY@@ bytes, headers @@HDR@@ bytes (@@HEAP@@ bytes in use), in the half-gcd stage. A stack bound of 65,536 bytes completes the total (the run was executed under a 64 KiB stack limit). The largest live set of the powering is the transform buffer (3 x 2^@@AEXP@@ elements), one transform row, the Barrett inverse, the modulus, the result and the twiddle table. The pages the kernel maps outside the executable image (vdso, vvar, page tables) are the kernel's memory. Cross-check: the maximum resident set of the run measured with GNU time was @@RSS@@ bytes."+n[j:]
rn("What is not included. Nothing","Scope of the claim. Nothing")
rn("The standard-library call that writes the encoded output text and the program's printing of its own counters are not counted; the allocator's instruction counts are not charged as time (its memory is counted in full). ","The report, its formatting and its one write call, and the allocator, are charged inside the total as stated above. The meter that records the charges (the counter increments) is how the rules are applied and is not a step of the program. ")
open('note_template.md','w').write(n)
b=open('build_package.py').read()
b=b.replace("'HEAP': L(HEAP),","'HEAP': L(HEAP), 'ARENA': L(ARENA), 'EXTENT': L(EXTENT),")
b=b.replace("The time is the executed total of one run of the shipped source, with every trial charged and the output stage included; no bound, estimate or other run enters it.","The time is the executed total of one run of the shipped source, with every trial charged and the allocator, the report formatting, the single write and the exit charged in stage I; the only bounds in it are the stated per-byte, per-stage and system-call constants of proof.md section 4.2, each charged in full.")
open('build_package.py','w').write(b)
